.TH IDLE\-HUNTER 1 "2026-09" "idle-hunter" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
idle-hunter \- find zombie AWS resources with a confidence-to-delete score
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B idle-hunter
.B scan
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Finds resources that are costing money and doing nothing \(em unattached EBS
volumes, unassociated Elastic IPs, load balancers with no targets \(em and
scores each one by how safe it looks to delete, rather than only listing it.
.PP
Nothing is ever deleted.
.B \-\-commands
prints the deletion commands for you to review and run.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B scan
Scan for zombie resources.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-region " REGION"
Region to scan.
.TP
.B \-\-all\-regions
Scan every region.
.TP
.BI \-\-min\-confidence " N"
Only report findings at or above this confidence.
.TP
.B \-\-commands
Print deletion commands. They are never executed.
.TP
.B \-\-live\-pricing
Look up real prices via the Pricing API. Needs
.BR pricing:GetProducts .
.TP
.BI \-\-workers " N"
Regions scanned in parallel with
.B \-\-all\-regions
(default 8). Lower it if the account is being throttled.
.TP
.B \-\-json
Machine-readable output.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
A scan completed.
.TP
.B non-zero
AWS could not be queried.
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
Scan one region:
.PP
.RS
.B idle-hunter scan \-\-region eu-west-1
.RE
.PP
Everywhere, only the confident findings, with the commands:
.PP
.RS
.B idle-hunter scan \-\-all\-regions \-\-min\-confidence 80 \-\-commands
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR cost-diff (1),
.BR iam-shrink (1).
Project documentation:
https://github.com/fabiocicerchia/idle-hunter
